{"id": "EUVD-2026-86890", "enisaUuid": "8c7bf4b0-220f-3b2e-aa3d-81cb9c5704ba", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nhwmon: (gpio-fan) Fix use-after-free in alarm work\n\nfan_alarm_irq_handler() queues fan_data->alarm_work, but nothing\ncancels it.  fan_alarm_notify() dereferences fan_data and its hwmon\ndevice.  On unbind, devres frees the interrupt, which only waits for\nthe handler itself, and then releases the hwmon device and fan_data,\nso a pending fan_alarm_notify() can run after those frees.\n\nReplace INIT_WORK() with devm_work_autocancel(), registered before\ndevm_request_irq().  The devres cleanup then frees the interrupt\nfirst, so no new work can be queued, and cancels the work while\nfan_data and the hwmon device are still alive.\n\nThis issue was found by an in-house static analysis tool.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:22:03", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:09:44", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/594c62eea7c82f526054496e9fa9b895122a8016", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6e67d9bdac810edacef78cbaeedd34445aa8ceb7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e9fc7d53b2eb34c0a607d1659f49b46911aaf16c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9b12bd724db9db318e3a68be17693583dc29a066", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/30755d3a5782cd704c8921cac8ee66dffe4383ea", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c6ab7f855891877a16d2e2ddf0cd0305fd098a85", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a2471ed17b0e6ff7bfb6b2ea8e6e5b04c309d293"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-97582", "GHSA-g5h6-rr2f-33x7"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2e596163-4842-3e94-8397-11280dc1d724", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "37efc222-680e-3716-8f94-44710b561ca5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "467f26f0-51e6-3172-b344-f026625410b9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "5b871c35-167e-34fa-a69f-b0bfd187616b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d6fe1360f42e86262153927986dea6502daff703 <a2471ed17b0e6ff7bfb6b2ea8e6e5b04c309d293"}, {"id": "5f890aa3-c3a3-3dc7-bdf2-8101a83c71e9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d6fe1360f42e86262153927986dea6502daff703 <6e67d9bdac810edacef78cbaeedd34445aa8ceb7"}, {"id": "60e8fd87-fffb-3a8d-83dd-f89a625dece1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "62e63b7b-6dd1-32aa-8c95-80c44dfeff9f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "7756716f-8354-38c3-a469-5b3387471267", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.222"}, {"id": "9b682434-4fcf-3165-a4d3-04d6444cbbf4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.189"}, {"id": "a275f2bd-52a2-326d-b6da-dab810773985", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d6fe1360f42e86262153927986dea6502daff703 <30755d3a5782cd704c8921cac8ee66dffe4383ea"}, {"id": "a6f5aa04-469f-39e4-989e-27c15ca78342", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.37"}, {"id": "b0758d67-2994-31ea-bad8-e07df3b690f9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d6fe1360f42e86262153927986dea6502daff703 <594c62eea7c82f526054496e9fa9b895122a8016"}, {"id": "b5f9b8d7-8487-31be-8309-f999234f981a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d6fe1360f42e86262153927986dea6502daff703 <e9fc7d53b2eb34c0a607d1659f49b46911aaf16c"}, {"id": "bf673592-a05d-39f7-9577-82a12118642d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d6fe1360f42e86262153927986dea6502daff703 <9b12bd724db9db318e3a